    "q-94359": {
      "dom_id": "step-q94359",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "The position $y(t)$ of a particle oscillating with light damped harmonic motion is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+10y=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. What is the period of the damped oscillation?",
      "worked_solution": "The given equation represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. We are looking for solutions of the form $y={e}^{\\lambda t}.$\n\nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +10=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +10 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +9)-9+10 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\lambda +3 & =\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-3\\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}={e}^{-3t}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡t).\n$$\n\nFrom the solution, the value of the angular frequency is $Ω=1\\,{\\text{s}}^{-1}.$\n\nThe period of the damped oscillation $T$ is related to the angular frequency as follows:\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{Ω}\n$$\n\nSo the period is\n\n$$\nT=2\\pi \\,\\text{s}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
